            "Registry address validation and zero-address handling",
            "Privilege escalation, role revocation, and upgrade-related access paths"
          ],
          "priority": 10,
          "reasoning": "WHY NOW: AccessController is a foundational permission component that seeds deployer roles and rejects a zero registry; flaws here could affect authorization across every vault, registry, factory, and integration. EXIT CRITERIA: Trace all role creation, assignment, revocation, admin, and registry-validation paths; verify initialization cannot be replayed or hijacked, unauthorized accounts cannot obtain privileged roles, and all dependent contracts enforce the intended roles without bypasses.",
          "category": "aspect",
          "expected_impact": "high"
        }
      ]
