      "items": [
        {
          "goal": "Vulnerability analysis of External oracle providers",
          "focus_areas": [
            "Signed answer validation and authorization of oracle responses",
            "Round ID, timestamp, freshness, and sequencer/staleness checks",
            "Answer denomination, decimal scaling, and negative or zero price handling",
            "Fallback behavior and resistance to manipulated or replayed signed data"
          ],
          "priority": 8,
          "reasoning": "WHY NOW: This is one of the two remaining unvisited nodes and directly supplies pricing data to vault and swap-related components, making validation failures potentially systemic. The component interfaces with external data and exposes signed answers, round timestamps, and round IDs, which are common sources of stale-price, replay, decimal, and trust-boundary vulnerabilities. EXIT CRITERIA: Confirm the complete trust and verification path for provider responses, including signer authorization, signature/domain binding, round monotonicity, freshness limits, answer bounds, denomination conversion, failure behavior, and whether all consumers enforce the required invariants; record any concrete exploitable gap or conclude that these checks are adequately enforced.",
          "category": "aspect",
          "expected_impact": "high"
        }
      ]
